  "body": "### Summary\nAs an MP user, I want to mark a conversation unread or delete it from the MP list itself, so that I do not have to open it first.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator, 2026-11-08). Found by the `2440d79..2fe43da3` sweep of #655.\n\n### Legacy @ `2fe43da3` (`legacy/duo-inner-cover`, AGENTS.md §2)\n- `4a4f493f` \"Add private message unread and delete actions\": context menu on an MP row, \"Marquer non lu\" on read rows only, \"Supprimer\" with a confirmation, then the row is removed locally (`HFRswift/Swift/MPListView.swift:810, 819`, confirmation `715`).\n- Mark unread: GET `user/nonlu.php` built by legacy from the topic id (`MPListView.swift:85-110`, URL at `92`).\n- Delete: POST `modo/manageaction.php` with `action_reaction=valid_eff_prive` (`MPListView.swift:140-158`), the request LOT-094 already ports.\n\n### Current SwiftHFR\nMark unread exists in the MP reader only (LOT-127 #218, GAP-116); LOT-127 states the list \"cannot\" do it because rows carry no `nonlu.php` link, but legacy builds the URL itself. Thread delete has its engine (LOT-094, closed) and its app lot in M5 (LOT-181 #421, GAP-117).\n\n### Scope\n- Context menu on MP rows: \"Marquer non lu\" (read rows only) and \"Supprimer\" (confirmation), reusing LOT-094's flow for delete.\n- The list-built `nonlu.php` URL: compare legacy's parameters with a capture before shipping; if none exists, open a capture issue (`host: mac`) and keep the entry behind it.\n- Coordinate with LOT-127 / LOT-181 (this may pull LOT-181's list part into M4: operator call).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Both entries appear only where legacy shows them; delete asks first; the row updates on HFR's confirmation (`unconfirmed` handled per LOT-048).\n- Tests on captured answers, loopback session only.",
